{
  "title": "HUL tells Delhi High Court it will remove Lakme sunscreen ad disparaging Derma Co",
  "publication_date": "2025-04-17T09:59:03Z",
  "summary": "Hindustan Unilever Limited told the Delhi High Court it will withdraw and republish Lakme sunscreen advertisements after removing references that allegedly disparage Honasa Consumer Limited\u2019s Derma Co brand.",
  "content": "Hindustan Unilever Limited (HUL), owner of the Lakme brand, informed the Delhi High Court on Thursday that it will withdraw and republish its Lakme sunscreen advertisements after removing references that allegedly disparage Honasa Consumer Limited\u2019s Derma Co brand.\n\nThe company said it would take down the current ads and issue revised versions without the contested references. HUL told the court the changes would address the complaints made by Honasa Consumer Limited regarding alleged disparagement of the Derma Co brand.\n\nThe matter was brought before the Delhi High Court, where HUL recorded its intention to modify and republish the advertisements rather than continue with the existing creative copy that prompted the dispute.\n\nThe report was originally published by Bar and Bench. Follow Us\n\nCopyright \u00a9 2021 Bar and Bench. All Rights Reserved\n\nPowered by Quintype",
